BEHAVIOR println-bytes

DESCRIPTION
  Writes length raw bytes from a buffer to standard output, followed by newline.
  For data that is a genuinely fixed `bytes` buffer carrying its length
  separately (e.g. a value read out of a key/value store slot) rather than a
  self-describing `string`. For strings, use println instead.
  A sink: writes the bytes, returns nothing.

CONTRACT
  INPUT data bytes 65536
  INPUT length int 8

HASH 2674dba0

NATIVE
